// The pairs of worker docs the per-project-scheduling migration deliberately
// forked, and which side is which. Data only — the rule that uses it lives in
// worker-doc-drift.mjs, and the pack test proves this list still matches the
// repo (every legacy `worker:` doc appears here; every path still exists).
//
// WHY THE SPLIT IS FORCED (docs/per-project-scheduling/MIGRATION.md, Phase 0):
// the task conversion is ADDITIVE, not a rename. Each pack grew a
// `tasks/<name>/task.md` (the executor-dispatched worker, per-repo access model)
// ALONGSIDE its untouched `run_daily` worker doc (the central planner's worker,
// fleet access model), so the legacy planner stays functional as the rollback
// until Phase 4 decommissions it. The two docs teach the SAME procedure in
// different dispatch dress, so their wording legitimately differs and no
// byte-identity guard can hold them together — only a "you edited one, edit the
// other" guard can.
//
// AT PHASE 4: `run_daily/` is deleted, and this file goes with it.
export const WORKER_DOC_PAIRS = [
  {
    legacy: 'packs/basics/run_daily/baselining.worker.md',
    task: 'packs/basics/tasks/baselining/task.md',
  },
  {
    legacy: 'packs/grow_with_claudinite/conversation-extract.md',
    task: 'packs/grow_with_claudinite/tasks/conversation-extract/task.md',
